    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10258" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">congestīcĭus</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-tĭus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		1. congero, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>brought together, heaped</i> or <i>piled up</i> (rare; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mostly post-Aug.): agger ex materiā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. C. 2, 15</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">materia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					2, 16, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">humus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					2, 10, 18</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">terra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pall. Sept. 7</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Oct. 11, 2</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">congesticius aut paluster locus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr.
					3, 4, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
